  "note": "The Egyptian oven word was borrowed from Semitic. Kilani, Vocalisation in Group Writing, p. 46, compares its spelling with Ugaritic tnrr. The interpretation of the Ugaritic passage as a noun is disputed. The database also groups the ear term תְּנוּךְ under the same index key."
